{
  "@context": "https://openvex.dev/ns/v0.2.0",
  "@id": "https://openvex.dev/docs/public/vex-fc1d5deddaa81550dea7f4a50b3975a7c18832da2d65abd5642934472389651d",
  "author": "Deckhouse <contact@deckhouse.io>",
  "version": 5,
  "statements": [
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://bdu.fstec.ru/vul/2025-09312",
        "description": "A vulnerability in the firewalld daemon, part of the Moby containerization framework, is related to improper resource initialization. Exploitation of this vulnerability could allow an attacker to gain unauthorized access to protected information.",
        "name": "CVE-2025-54410",
        "aliases": [
          "BDU:2025-09312"
        ]
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/docker/docker@v27.1.1+incompatible"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/docker/docker@v27.3.1+incompatible"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path",
      "impact_statement": "Moby is an open source container framework developed by Docker Inc. that is distributed as Docker Engine, Mirantis Container Runtime, and various other downstream projects/products. A firewalld firewall controller daemon vulnerability affects Moby releases before 28.0.0. When firewalld reloads, Docker fails to re-create iptables rules that isolate bridge networks, allowing any container to access all ports on any other container across different bridge networks on the same host. Deckhouse Kubernetes Platform is not vulnerable as it does not use this functionality for container isolation.",
      "timestamp": "2025-10-14T11:19:11.56805Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-34040",
        "description": "AuthZ plugin bypass with oversized request body",
        "name": "CVE-2026-34040",
        "aliases": [
          "GHSA-x744-4wpc-v9h2"
        ]
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/docker/docker@v27.1.1+incompatible"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/docker/docker@v27.3.1+incompatible"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path",
      "impact_statement": "Moby is an open source container framework. Prior to version 29.3.1, a security vulnerability has been detected that allows attackers to bypass authorization plugins (AuthZ). Deckhouse Kubernetes Platform is not affected as it does not rely on these plugins in any way and does not ship them.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-17T12:23:32Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-15558",
        "description": "Privilege escalation in Docker CLI and Desktop",
        "name": "CVE-2025-15558",
        "aliases": [
          "ZDI-CAN-28304"
        ]
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/docker/docker@v27.1.1+incompatible"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/docker/docker@v27.2.1+incompatible"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/docker/cli@v27.1.1+incompatible"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/docker/cli@v29.0.3+incompatible"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/docker/cli@v29.0.3%2Bincompatible"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/docker/cli"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path",
      "impact_statement": "Docker CLI for Windows searches for plugin binaries in C:\\ProgramData\\Docker\\cli-plugins, a directory that does not exist by default. A low-privileged attacker can create this directory and place malicious CLI plugin binaries (docker-compose.exe, docker-buildx.exe, etc.) that are executed when a victim user opens Docker Desktop or invokes Docker CLI plugin features, and allow privilege-escalation if the docker CLI is executed as a privileged user. This issue does affect Deckhouse Kubernetes Platform because it does not use or ship Docker.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-17T12:23:32Z",
      "last_updated": "2026-09-07T12:30:00Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-22703",
        "description": "Verification accepts any valid Rekor entry under certain conditions",
        "name": "CVE-2026-22703",
        "aliases": [
          "GHSA-whqx-f9j3-ch6m"
        ]
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/sigstore/cosign/v2@v2.2.4"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path",
      "impact_statement": "Prior to versions 2.6.2 and 3.0.4, Cosign bundle can be crafted to successfully verify an artifact even if the embedded Rekor entry does not reference the artifact's digest, signature or public key. When verifying a Rekor entry, Cosign verifies the Rekor entry signature, and also compares the artifact's digest, the user's public key from either a Fulcio certificate or provided by the user, and the artifact signature to the Rekor entry contents. Without these comparisons, Cosign would accept any response from Rekor as valid. A malicious actor that has compromised a user's identity or signing key could construct a valid Cosign bundle by including any arbitrary Rekor entry, thus preventing the user from being able to audit the signing event. This issue has been patched in versions 2.6.2 and 3.0.4. Deckhouse Kubernetes Platform is not vulnerable as it does not utilize cosign bundles for verification.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-01T14:34:03Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-24137",
        "description": "Legacy TUF client allows for arbitrary file writes with target cache path traversal",
        "name": "CVE-2026-24137",
        "aliases": [
          "GHSA-fcv2-xgw5-pqxf"
        ]
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/sigstore/sigstore@v1.8.3"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path",
      "impact_statement": "In versions 1.10.3 and below, the legacy TUF client (pkg/tuf/client.go) supports caching target files to disk. It constructs a filesystem path by joining a cache base directory with a target name sourced from signed target metadata; however, it does not validate that the resulting path stays within the cache base directory. A malicious TUF repository can trigger arbitrary file overwriting, limited to the permissions that the calling process has. Note that this should only affect clients that are directly using the TUF client in sigstore/sigstore or are using an older version of Cosign. Public Sigstore deployment users are unaffected, as TUF metadata is validated by a quorum of trusted collaborators. This issue has been fixed in version 1.10.4. Deckhouse Kubernetes Platform is not affected by this since it does not rely on any TUF repositories or Cosign.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-01T14:34:03Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-24117",
        "description": "Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) via provided public key URL",
        "name": "CVE-2026-24117",
        "aliases": [
          "GHSA-4c4x-jm2x-pf9j"
        ]
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/sigstore/rekor@v1.3.6"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path",
      "impact_statement": "In versions 1.4.3 and below, attackers can trigger SSRF to arbitrary internal services because /api/v1/index/retrieve supports retrieving a public key via user-provided URL. Since the SSRF only can trigger GET requests, the request cannot mutate state. The response from the GET request is not returned to the caller so data exfiltration is not possible. A malicious actor could attempt to probe an internal network through Blind SSRF. The issue has been fixed in version 1.5.0. Deckhouse Kubernetes Platform is not affected since it does not utilize rekor.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-01T14:34:03Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-66564",
        "description": "Excessive memory allocation during request parsing",
        "name": "CVE-2025-66564",
        "aliases": [
          "GHSA-4qg8-fj49-pxjh"
        ]
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/sigstore/timestamp-authority@v1.2.2"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path",
      "impact_statement": "Prior to 2.0.3, Function api.ParseJSONRequest currently splits (via a call to strings.Split) an optionally-provided OID (which is untrusted data) on periods. Similarly, function api.getContentType splits the Content-Type header (which is also untrusted data) on an application string. As a result, in the face of a malicious request with either an excessively long OID in the payload containing many period characters or a malformed Content-Type header, a call to api.ParseJSONRequest or api.getContentType incurs allocations of O(n) bytes (where n stands for the length of the function's argument). Deckhouse Kubernetes Platform is not affected by this since it does not implement or rely on timestamp verification using this package.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-01T14:34:03Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-33747",
        "description": "Malicious frontend can cause file escape outside of storage root",
        "name": "CVE-2026-33747",
        "aliases": [
          "GHSA-4c29-8rgm-jvjj"
        ]
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/moby/buildkit@v0.16.0"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/moby/buildkit@v0.15.1"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_present",
      "impact_statement": "BuildKit is a toolkit for converting source code to build artifacts in an efficient, expressive and repeatable manner. Prior to version 0.28.1, when using a custom BuildKit frontend, the frontend can craft an API message that causes files to be written outside of the BuildKit state directory for the execution context. Deckhouse Kubernetes Platform is not affected by this since it does not ship or utilize Buildkit.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-17T12:23:32Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-33748",
        "description": "Git URL subdir component can cause access to restricted files",
        "name": "CVE-2026-33748",
        "aliases": [
          "GHSA-4vrq-3vrq-g6gg"
        ]
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/moby/buildkit@v0.16.0"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/moby/buildkit@v0.15.1"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_present",
      "impact_statement": "BuildKit is a toolkit for converting source code to build artifacts in an efficient, expressive and repeatable manner. Prior to version 0.28.1, insufficient validation of Git URL fragment subdir components may allow access to files outside the checked-out Git repository root. Possible access is limited to files on the same mounted filesystem. Deckhouse Kubernetes Platform is not affected by this since it does not ship or utilize Buildkit.",
      "timestamp": "2026-05-16T12:31:20Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-23831",
        "description": "COSE v0.0.1 entry type nil pointer dereference in Canonicalize via empty Message",
        "name": "CVE-2026-23831",
        "aliases": [
          "GHSA-273p-m2cw-6833"
        ]
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/sigstore/rekor@v1.3.6"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path",
      "impact_statement": "Rekor is a software supply chain transparency log. In versions 1.4.3 and below, the entry implementation can panic on attacker-controlled input when canonicalizing a proposed entry with an empty spec.message, causing nil Pointer Dereference. Function validate() returns nil (success) when message is empty, leaving sign1Msg uninitialized, and Canonicalize() later dereferences v.sign1Msg.Payload. A malformed proposed entry of the cose/v0.0.1 type can cause a panic on a thread within the Rekor process. The thread is recovered so the client receives a 500 error message and service still continues, so the availability impact of this is minimal. Deckhouse Kubernetes Platform is not vulnerable since it does not utilize rekor in any way.",
      "timestamp": "2026-05-16T12:31:20Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-33997",
        "description": "Off-by-one error in plugin privilege validation",
        "name": "CVE-2026-33997",
        "aliases": [
          "GHSA-pxq6-2prw-chj9"
        ]
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/docker/docker@v27.1.1+incompatible"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/docker/docker@v27.3.1+incompatible"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path",
      "impact_statement": "Prior to version 29.3.1, a security vulnerability has been detected that allows plugins privilege validation to be bypassed during docker plugin install. Due to an error in the daemon's privilege comparison logic, the daemon may incorrectly accept a privilege set that differs from the one approved by the user. Plugins that request exactly one privilege are also affected, because no comparison is performed at all. This issue has been patched in version 29.3.1. Deckhouse Kubernetes Platform is not affeceted by this since it does not ship or use Docker daemon or it's plugins in any way.",
      "timestamp": "2026-05-16T12:31:20Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-41567",
        "description": "Docker: PUT /containers/{id}/archive executes container binary on the host",
        "name": "CVE-2026-41567"
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/docker/docker@v27.1.1+incompatible"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/docker/docker@v27.3.1+incompatible"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path",
      "impact_statement": "The vulnerability affects Docker daemon archive extraction behavior. Deckhouse Kubernetes Platform is not affected because it does not ship or use Docker daemon API endpoints in this execution path for operator-trivy and trivy binaries.",
      "timestamp": "2026-06-19T14:09:00Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-42306",
        "description": "Docker vulnerability affecting github.com/docker/docker.",
        "name": "CVE-2026-42306"
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/docker/docker@v27.1.1+incompatible"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/docker/docker@v27.3.1+incompatible"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path",
      "impact_statement": "Deckhouse Kubernetes Platform is not affected because operator-trivy components are Go binaries and do not run or expose Docker daemon code paths required to trigger this vulnerability.",
      "timestamp": "2026-06-22T14:37:00Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-41568",
        "description": "Docker vulnerability affecting github.com/docker/docker.",
        "name": "CVE-2026-41568"
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/docker/docker@v27.1.1+incompatible"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/docker/docker@v27.3.1+incompatible"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path",
      "impact_statement": "Deckhouse Kubernetes Platform is not affected because operator-trivy components are Go binaries and do not run or expose Docker daemon code paths required to trigger this vulnerability.",
      "timestamp": "2026-06-22T14:40:00Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-5932",
        "description": "The golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp package is unmaintained, unsafe by design, and has known security issues that will not be fixed.",
        "name": "GO-2026-5932"
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/golang.org/x/crypto"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/golang.org/x/crypto@v0.50.0"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/golang.org/x/crypto@v0.55.0"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path",
      "impact_statement": "GO-2026-5932 affects unmaintained golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp with no fixed version. The operator-trivy trivy binary only uses other x/crypto subpackages; openpgp is not imported or executed.",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-03T12:00:00Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-46600",
        "description": "Panic when parsing malformed SVCB/HTTPS DNS resource records in golang.org/x/net/dns/dnsmessage.",
        "name": "CVE-2026-46600"
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/golang.org/x/net"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/golang.org/x/net@v0.53.0"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/golang.org/x/net@v0.57.0"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path",
      "impact_statement": "CVE-2026-46600 is in golang.org/x/net/dns/dnsmessage SVCB/HTTPS RR parsing. The operator-trivy trivy binary does not parse untrusted DNS messages via dnsmessage; name resolution uses the standard Go/OS resolver. The vulnerable code path is not reachable.",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-03T12:00:00Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39824",
        "description": "NewNTUnicodeString in golang.org/x/sys/windows does not check for string length overflow.",
        "name": "CVE-2026-39824"
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/golang.org/x/sys"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/golang.org/x/sys@v0.43.0"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/golang.org/x/sys@v0.47.0"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_present",
      "impact_statement": "CVE-2026-39824 affects golang.org/x/sys/windows (NewNTUnicodeString). The operator-trivy trivy binary is built with GOOS=linux; windows-tagged sources are excluded by build constraints and are not present in the Linux artifact.",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-03T12:00:00Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-56852",
        "description": "DoS via infinite loop in golang.org/x/text unicode/norm when processing invalid UTF-8.",
        "name": "CVE-2026-56852"
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/golang.org/x/text"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/golang.org/x/text@v0.36.0"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/golang.org/x/text@v0.41.0"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_cannot_be_controlled_by_adversary",
      "impact_statement": "CVE-2026-56852 is in golang.org/x/text/unicode/norm. In the operator-trivy trivy binary, norm is only reached indirectly (for example via IDNA host normalization) on trusted registry/API hostnames, not on adversary-controlled arbitrary UTF-8 payloads. The vulnerable path is not adversary-controlled.",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-03T12:00:00Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "name": "CVE-2026-27145",
        "description": "crypto/x509: Denial of Service via excessive processing of DNS SAN entries"
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/stdlib@v1.25.8"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_cannot_be_controlled_by_adversary",
      "impact_statement": "crypto/x509: Denial of Service via excessive processing of DNS SAN entries. The trivy image is built with Go stdlib v1.25.8 (Deckhouse builder golang:1.25.8, GOTOOLCHAIN=local). A fix requires bumping the Go toolchain above the builder version; this will be done as part of the planned builder image upgrade. In the current module configuration, inputs to vulnerable stdlib paths are limited to trusted control-plane/administrative scenarios, which excludes practical exploitation by an untrusted attacker.",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-07T12:00:00Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "name": "CVE-2026-32280",
        "description": "crypto/x509, crypto/tls: Denial of Service in certificate chain building"
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/stdlib@v1.25.8"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_cannot_be_controlled_by_adversary",
      "impact_statement": "crypto/x509, crypto/tls: Denial of Service in certificate chain building. The trivy image is built with Go stdlib v1.25.8 (Deckhouse builder golang:1.25.8, GOTOOLCHAIN=local). A fix requires bumping the Go toolchain above the builder version; this will be done as part of the planned builder image upgrade. In the current module configuration, inputs to vulnerable stdlib paths are limited to trusted control-plane/administrative scenarios, which excludes practical exploitation by an untrusted attacker.",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-07T12:00:00Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "name": "CVE-2026-32281",
        "description": "crypto/x509: Denial of Service via inefficient certificate chain validation"
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/stdlib@v1.25.8"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_cannot_be_controlled_by_adversary",
      "impact_statement": "crypto/x509: Denial of Service via inefficient certificate chain validation. The trivy image is built with Go stdlib v1.25.8 (Deckhouse builder golang:1.25.8, GOTOOLCHAIN=local). A fix requires bumping the Go toolchain above the builder version; this will be done as part of the planned builder image upgrade. In the current module configuration, inputs to vulnerable stdlib paths are limited to trusted control-plane/administrative scenarios, which excludes practical exploitation by an untrusted attacker.",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-07T12:00:00Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "name": "CVE-2026-32282",
        "description": "internal/syscall/unix: Root.Chmod can follow symlinks out of the root"
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/stdlib@v1.25.8"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_cannot_be_controlled_by_adversary",
      "impact_statement": "internal/syscall/unix: Root.Chmod can follow symlinks out of the root. The trivy image is built with Go stdlib v1.25.8 (Deckhouse builder golang:1.25.8, GOTOOLCHAIN=local). A fix requires bumping the Go toolchain above the builder version; this will be done as part of the planned builder image upgrade. In the current module configuration, inputs to vulnerable stdlib paths are limited to trusted control-plane/administrative scenarios, which excludes practical exploitation by an untrusted attacker.",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-07T12:00:00Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "name": "CVE-2026-32283",
        "description": "crypto/tls: Denial of Service via multiple TLS 1.3 key update messages"
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/stdlib@v1.25.8"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_cannot_be_controlled_by_adversary",
      "impact_statement": "crypto/tls: Denial of Service via multiple TLS 1.3 key update messages. The trivy image is built with Go stdlib v1.25.8 (Deckhouse builder golang:1.25.8, GOTOOLCHAIN=local). A fix requires bumping the Go toolchain above the builder version; this will be done as part of the planned builder image upgrade. In the current module configuration, inputs to vulnerable stdlib paths are limited to trusted control-plane/administrative scenarios, which excludes practical exploitation by an untrusted attacker.",
